{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>It is better that I give her to you.</b> Our Rabbi Hananel explained: even though giving her to another man is the case, it is better — for a woman cannot be without a man, nor a man without a woman, in the manner of what is written (Genesis 2:18): ״לא טוב היות האדם לבדו״. 'You are better than your fellow' — and this is two good things, one better than the other. And further we find two bad things, one better than its fellow (Lamentations 4:9): ״טובים היו חללי חרב מחללי רעב״. And further we find two things, one good and the second lesser (Ecclesiastes 4:13): ״טוב ילד מסכן וחכם ממלך זקן וכסיל״. And one better than its fellow (Proverbs 15:17): ״טוב ארחת ירק ואהבה שם משור אבוס ושנאה בו״. And further, two good things, and there is a third better than both of them (Ecclesiastes 5:4): ״טוב אשר לא תדור משתדור ולא תשלם״ — and better than both of them is one who vows and fulfills. And like it (Ecclesiastes 4:2–3): ״ושבח אני את המתים שכבר מתו מן החיים אשר המה חיים עדנה״ — and better than both of them: ״את אשר עדן לא היה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:14.979721935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}